   ("p", "Binary code is the language computers actually think in: every character you type, every pixel on this screen and every file on your disk is, at the lowest level, a pattern of ones and zeros. Converting text to binary makes that hidden layer visible, and it is far simpler than it looks once you know the two ideas behind it. This guide explains what binary is, how a letter becomes a byte, and how to convert text to binary and back reliably. You can follow along with the free <a href=\"../tools/binary-code-translator.html\">Binary Code Translator</a>, which runs entirely in your browser."),
