   ("p", "Knowing the patterns is only half of Morse. The other half is timing, because the gaps carry as much meaning as the marks. Everything is measured in one basic unit of time, and the rules are fixed: a dot is one unit, a dash is three units, the gap between symbols within a letter is one unit, the gap between letters is three units, and the gap between words is seven units. Get the spacing wrong and HELLO can dissolve into gibberish even if every individual dot and dash is correct."),
