   ("p", "Morse speed is measured in words per minute, and it is standardised using the reference word PARIS, which is exactly 50 units long including its spacing. At 15 words per minute you are sending 750 units every minute, so each unit lasts 80 milliseconds. Raise the speed and every dot, dash and gap shrinks proportionally. Experienced operators comfortably read 20 to 30 words per minute; contest operators go much faster. The translator lets you drag a speed slider so you can start slow and speed up as your ear adjusts."),
